# Copy to .env.local.
#
# IMPORTANT: .env.local must be UTF-8. Windows PowerShell 5.1 writes UTF-16 LE
# with a BOM when you use `>`, which the dotenv parser reads as UTF-8: the
# variable name comes back mangled, the key is never seen, and the assistant
# quietly serves its FAQ fallback forever — a working site with a dead
# assistant, and nothing in the logs to say so. Write it with
# `Set-Content -Encoding utf8` or from a POSIX shell.

# Canonical origin. Everything absolute resolves against it: metadataBase,
# Open Graph, the sitemap, robots.txt and every JSON-LD @id.
# Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Optional. Without it the assistant still answers — /api/chat falls back to a
# keyword search over the published FAQ and never returns an error. The key
# only makes it better.
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=""

# Optional. Defaults to gemini-3.5-flash.
# Note: the 3.x series counts reasoning against maxOutputTokens, which is why
# the route sets thinkingLevel "minimal" rather than thinkingBudget (2.5 only).
ASSISTANT_MODEL="gemini-3.5-flash"
